  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MSI Core Contribution 2023-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MSI&apos;s impact goals is to ensure that women and girls, including the most vulnerable and hardest-to-reach, have increased health, wellbeing, and gender equality. MSI brings an added value to Norad&#x2019;s SRHR portfolio, both when it comes to their role as a service provider and as a partner providing linkages (local to global) and context. 

This is supported  two interconnected outcomes: 
- Outcome 1 on improved access for women, girls, and youth in all their diversities
- Outcome 2 on an improved enabling environment. 

The former is reached through addressing both supply side barriers and gaps to access (e.g. trainings and service delivery to strengthen quality of care for target groups) and demand side barriers (challenging gender and social norms that restrict access), while the latter is achieved by combining MSI advocacy and technical expertise to influence government authorities and service providers both from within and via external channels.</narrative>
  </description>
